WEBVTT

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:35.780
You have ninety minutes to answer the prompt. You may leave when you're finished.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:52.890
This job is your last resort, isn't it?

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:56.140
Oh, no. I'm taking it very seriously.

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:06.280
Even if you are accepted, do you plan to
decline the offer if you're to be stationed at sales?

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:11.860
No, that won't be a problem.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:16.240
Sales... In my opinion, sales is a very fulfilling line of work.

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:18.400
If you're willing to provide me with an
opportunity,
I wouldn't hesitate to accept.

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:23.300
<i>Who am I trying to convince?</i>

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:35.680
For the past four years,

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:38.880
I've been particularly conscious of how people communicate with each other through the volunteer work I've done.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:48.280
The reason I chose to apply for a job at this publishing company was because I believe I have a lot to offer the editing section.

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:52.440
You, the one with the smile on his face,

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:54.520
let's hear about why you applied for this job.

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:02.700
I wasn't... I mean, I was never a diligent university student.

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:07.660
My life in college was virtually a moratorium of sorts.

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:10.130
However, there was a moment in time...

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:19.190
Oh, excuse me. There was a moment in
time when I truly felt compelled to do something.

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:35.360
That is why I am seeking a job in this field.

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:40.400
Do you have any friends? Girlfriends?

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:47.400
Yes, I do.

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:48.630
Really?

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:52.550
In that case,
what do they think is the most attractive thing about you?

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:54.370
Attractive?

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:09.500
Yes, this is Sasahara Kanji.

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:13.180
Yes, yes. I'm happy to make your acquaintance.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:19.160
Oh, I see.

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:23.240
Okay, thank you very much. Okay, good-bye.

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:37.120
Hello?

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:40.220
What's up? Yeah, I'm on my way over there.

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:48.900
I'm back.

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:50.950
Good work. How was it?

00:04:57.670 --> 00:04:59.950
I finally persuaded Miyata-san.

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:02.650
I think the production line has been secured.

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:03.850
That's great!

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:08.080
It seems like I haven't been inside your room in ages, Kousaka.

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:09.670
Is that so?

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:21.150
Were you playing an ero-game the whole time?

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:22.780
Not the whole time.

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:26.900
Sorry I haven't been able to do it in a while.

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:28.820
No, it's okay.

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:30.730
<i>Does that mean...</i>

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:33.940
You don't need me as long as you have an ero-game?

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:34.480
Yeah.

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:42.800
What exactly am I to you, Kousaka?

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:46.650
Well, when it comes down to it,
it feels better when you do it yourself.

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:51.120
Men will only feel ecstasy for a
moment when they're with their partners.

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:56.260
Until that moment, men have to rely on
sights and sounds to build up their emotions.

00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:58.670
In other words, the brain is ultimately
responsible for creating a feeling of ecstasy.

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:00.630
That's why the conditions for attaining
that feeling are complicated in real life.

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:05.300
<i>Here... Please... Down here... More... More...</i>

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:11.000
Two-dimensional titles only require your
imagination to process the information on the screen,

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:12.470
which is why it's a more pure and sophisticated medium.

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:16.110
Oh, this isn't just about you, Saki-chan.

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:19.870
It's what I've concluded from my experience
with women in general, including you, Saki-chan.

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:22.790
If I had to choose between the two,

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:25.940
I'd choose something two-dimensional!

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:33.930
<i>Wow, it was a dream.</i>

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:35.680
<i>What a terrible dream.</i>

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:37.200
<i>It seemed so real.</i>

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:39.370
<i>I'm probably just tired.</i>

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:42.170
<i>It's true that I haven't been able to see Kousaka lately.</i>

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:50.640
Kousaka said he was going to apply for a job at
a game developer. I haven't seen him in a while.

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:51.930
Are you serious?

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:52.510
Which ones?

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:54.600
He told me, but I forgot what he said.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:57.110
It's not like I'd recognize them anyway.

00:06:57.110 --> 00:06:58.450
He mentioned several.

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:00.320
I wonder where he applied. Are they in Tokyo?

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:04.510
There are a lot of game developers
located in rural areas like Kansai and Kyuushuu.

00:07:04.930 --> 00:07:05.510
No way.

00:07:05.890 --> 00:07:07.200
I think they're in Tokyo.

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:12.100
It might be an industry giant like Oval or Vep.

00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:15.830
I'm happy that he's serious about finding work, but...

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:19.040
I don't think they hire people
based on how well they play games.

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:23.380
Well, I don't think that's why Kousaka-kun's applying.

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:25.780
Sasayan, you're trying to get a job at a
publishing company, right? How's that going?

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:28.630
It's pretty tough.

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:32.200
I've been trying since last year, but I haven't had any luck.

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:33.710
I see.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:37.050
Kasukabe-san, I heard you're going to open an apparel shop.

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:37.740
How's that going?

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:43.610
I've recently realized that you need to
gather people in order to make money.

00:07:44.010 --> 00:07:46.120
You sound like an entrepreneur.

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:49.200
You're the type of person who'd rather own
a store than work for somebody else, after all.

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:52.290
Well, there are struggles to be found regardless of what you do.

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:56.120
Exhausted?

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:57.070
A little.

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:02.430
Oh, Ogi, long time no see!

00:08:02.810 --> 00:08:04.560
Hello, it's been awhile.

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:12.730
Don't mix this kind of thing in with the rest!

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:15.600
Oh, you didn't like it?

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:19.120
Hiding personal favorites between
the others is typical otaku behavior.

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:21.440
How could this possibly serve as reference?

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:23.710
Now, now. Think of it as a source for ideas.

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:24.990
It's completely unnecessary!

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:27.860
Come on, there's no need to say that.

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:32.270
It's entirely different from the original title.

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:33.880
I personally can't stand it.

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:35.940
Doesn't that mean you looked through it?

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:37.870
Ah—no...

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:40.260
I-In any case, I'm returning it to you.

00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:42.050
Come on, don't say that.

00:08:42.050 --> 00:08:42.470
You have to get a feel for it with your heart.

00:08:42.470 --> 00:08:44.090
It seems like they're getting along.

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:44.360
You have to get a feel for it with your heart.

00:08:45.350 --> 00:08:46.110
Who knows?

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:48.560
Note the skillful old man and the power of his well-seasoned glare.

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:50.220
Stop it!

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:56.880
Is that reference material for the Comifes?

00:08:56.880 --> 00:08:59.130
No, this is something else.

00:08:59.130 --> 00:09:00.890
Are you going to draw a homo manga?

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:03.780
Yes, I am.

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:05.880
By the way, Sasahara,

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:10.850
I thought you were going to be a vendor at
the Comifes, but aren't you busy looking for a job?

00:09:11.810 --> 00:09:12.960
Yeah, I might be.

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:18.120
Well, you don't have to force
yourself if you're busy, Sasahara-san.

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:20.300
We'll see.

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:24.170
It'd help if there were three people, though.

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:25.180
That's true.
<i>Could it be...</i>

00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:26.280
Very true.
<i>Could it be...</i>

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:27.820
<i>Could it be...</i>

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:35.220
Sasahara-san and Ogiue-san?

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:38.760
Yeah. Don't you think there's
something going on between them?

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:40.430
Really?

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:44.140
Well, Sasahara-san is always kind to others,

00:09:44.510 --> 00:09:46.900
nothing more and nothing less.

00:09:46.900 --> 00:09:49.850
Wow, what inadvertent criticism.

00:09:49.850 --> 00:09:51.590
Besides, Ogiue-san's...

00:09:53.270 --> 00:09:53.860
Never mind.

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:56.340
<i>moe over Sasa x Mada, after all.</i>

00:09:57.490 --> 00:10:00.470
<i>Did she give up on the love triangle and focus on Sasahara?</i>

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:08.040
It's not like I'm in a position to be
worried about the welfare of others.

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:10.840
Did something happen between you and Kousaka-san?

00:10:11.810 --> 00:10:13.740
No, it's not that.

00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:15.390
We're just really busy these days.

00:10:15.740 --> 00:10:17.510
Oh, I see.

00:10:20.210 --> 00:10:22.550
<i>Well, I guess I don't have a choice.</i>

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:25.900
Hey, does Tanaka play ero-games?

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:28.060
Why'd you bring that up all of a sudden?

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:31.280
Does he not play them or do you ask him not to?

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:32.810
I don't ask him to do that.

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:34.620
It's more like we play them together.

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:38.490
I mean... He probably does it,
just like everyone else.

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:39.570
Why do you ask?

00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:40.910
Well...

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:47.130
It feels so good!

00:10:50.340 --> 00:10:51.830
Never mind.

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:53.820
I don't think I can use you as a reference.

00:10:54.620 --> 00:11:00.100
Does the cosplay event you attend
every week also serve as a date with Tanaka?

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:01.060
Well, yes.

00:11:01.480 --> 00:11:03.580
That must be fun.

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:05.130
What's that supposed to mean?

00:11:05.130 --> 00:11:07.480
Hi there, folks!

00:11:10.320 --> 00:11:12.770
Even more enthusiastic than usual, huh?

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:15.940
I recommend we go camping
during the summer!

00:11:15.940 --> 00:11:17.360
What show is that from?

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:20.980
Parody? Rip off? Homage?

00:11:20.980 --> 00:11:24.120
I wouldn't have expected to hear you say
anything about camping during the summer.

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:25.740
I feel insulted!

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:28.670
Did you get that idea from
yesterday's Motekano?

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:29.660
Uh-oh!

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:30.790
What's that?

00:11:31.350 --> 00:11:32.430
Not another manga, is it?

00:11:32.430 --> 00:11:34.080
I got it. It's probably that.

00:11:34.470 --> 00:11:37.950
It's the episode where they go on a date in the prairie.
It was a popular scene in the original version, too.

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:44.020
It was a story about a heartbroken protagonist who
checks into a hotel and is reunited with the woman he loves.

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:48.560
Are you saying you got the urge to
go camping after reading a manga?

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:50.020
Are you really that stupid?

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:55.990
Yes, I'm that stupid.

00:11:56.310 --> 00:11:57.070
Get lost!

00:11:57.070 --> 00:12:00.110
That aside, what were you expecting to get out
of a Motekano adaptation with these members?

00:12:00.520 --> 00:12:03.780
It'll be like a pilgrimage to the holy land!

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:09.430
Ishiwatari Hot Springs, Kazura Bridge, and watching the sunset from the lookout post, just to name a few.

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:14.870
Get out of here!

00:12:14.870 --> 00:12:16.740
Why don't you go by yourself?

00:12:16.740 --> 00:12:19.130
Trying to do something as a group is pretty pathetic.

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:22.540
What's wrong with going as a group? I want to go with everybody!

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:26.100
Everyone's busy looking for jobs and writing their dissertations.

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:30.070
The only people who can go are Ohno, Ogiue,

00:12:30.070 --> 00:12:31.600
No, I still have a script to write.

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:33.310
and you.

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:34.980
That sounds like a complete disaster.

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:37.610
Shock!

00:12:39.490 --> 00:12:42.820
Even if we could go,
it'd be better to wait until everyone settles down,

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:44.700
not that I'd go either way.

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:47.590
No! Never! The summer of summers!

00:12:47.590 --> 00:12:48.450
Do you really have nothing else to do?

00:12:48.900 --> 00:12:54.000
Settle down? That means those of us
who haven't found jobs won't be able to go.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:55.910
Well, why don't you just go?

00:12:56.340 --> 00:12:57.810
There's no harm in having a little fun.

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:01.310
<i>Besides, Kousaka definitely wouldn't be
eligible to go according to those conditions.</i>

00:13:01.310 --> 00:13:03.110
I hope you find a job soon.

00:13:03.110 --> 00:13:03.960
Yeah.

00:13:05.170 --> 00:13:07.260
This isn't fun! This isn't fun!

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:09.080
You guys don't want to because you've already done it!

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:14.240
I want to experience an exciting summer at least once!

00:13:14.760 --> 00:13:19.080
If I find a job, I'll be able to go camping
and to the Comifes without any qualms.

00:13:20.180 --> 00:13:22.080
You don't have to worry about that.

00:13:23.450 --> 00:13:25.430
Well, I did say that I'd help.

00:13:26.730 --> 00:13:28.310
You can forget about that promise.

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:31.630
No, no. I can't do that.

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:34.000
Sasa x Ogi!

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:37.460
Just kidding! I'm going to piss somebody off again!

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:44.020
As the man who discovered the Oh x Tana affair,
I foolishly thought that Sasa x Ogi was a possibility, too.

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:49.110
Yay! It was just my imagination running wild.
Sasa x Ogi, huh? It could happen!

00:13:49.490 --> 00:13:50.660
What do you think, Ogichin?

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:52.120
Who and who?

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:54.960
Sasa x Ogi. Ogi x Sasa?

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:57.290
There's no way I'd go out with an otaku!

00:14:03.990 --> 00:14:06.820
Nyo? It feels like there's a lot of tension in the air.

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:09.780
You'd definitely be the reckless type of comedian.

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:13.010
Well, that aside...

00:14:13.760 --> 00:14:16.080
Yeah, let's put that aside for now.

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:19.300
If there's one thing I've learned,

00:14:19.300 --> 00:14:21.760
it's that dating an otaku can be difficu...

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:25.300
Hello!

00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:27.560
Oh, K-Kousaka!

00:14:27.560 --> 00:14:28.640
Hi, Saki-chan!

00:14:28.640 --> 00:14:29.590
Long time no see!

00:14:30.040 --> 00:14:30.930
Hello.

00:14:31.740 --> 00:14:34.890
Hey, Saki-chan, I found a job.

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:37.360
You're kidding! Really? Where?

00:14:37.360 --> 00:14:38.690
Is it with the game company you wanted to work for?

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:40.020
Congratulations!

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:41.190
Thanks.

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:43.650
It's with a company called Pushke.

00:14:47.710 --> 00:14:48.530
Is it well known?

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:50.580
It's not like I'd know either way, though.

00:14:50.580 --> 00:14:52.400
I don't think I should be the one to explain it.

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:54.620
Me neither.

00:14:55.840 --> 00:14:57.660
You could say it's a famous company.

00:15:04.940 --> 00:15:05.950
<i>It couldn't be...</i>

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:07.050
It's an ero-game developer.

00:15:10.140 --> 00:15:12.350
<i>I thought so!</i>

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:19.440
The new title they're currently working on is
behind schedule, so I'll be working nights from now on.

00:15:19.950 --> 00:15:21.540
Their programmer ran away,

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:23.250
and I'm serving as his replacement.

00:15:23.960 --> 00:15:27.940
Programmer?
Kousaka-kun, do you know anything about programming?

00:15:28.730 --> 00:15:31.910
I didn't, but I studied it intensively for a month.

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:33.730
One month?

00:15:33.730 --> 00:15:35.590
I thought it'd be important to have those kinds of skills.

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:37.070
<i>Amazing.</i>

00:15:37.070 --> 00:15:38.330
<i>I envy him.</i>

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:43.750
<i>Poor Saki-san...
I don't understand why they haven't broken up yet.</i>

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:48.640
That's why I don't know when I'll have any
free time.
They're desperately in need of help.

00:15:48.970 --> 00:15:51.180
See what I mean?

00:15:51.730 --> 00:15:55.130
I don't think this is a matter about otakus anymore.

00:15:55.600 --> 00:16:01.490
Poor girl, how painful, poor girl,
how painful, poor girl, how painful, poor pain...

00:16:03.890 --> 00:16:06.980
We're going to a hotel right now!
A hotel, Kousaka!

00:16:07.810 --> 00:16:10.860
I already told you I had to work tonight, Saki-chan.

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:14.860
We're going to do it until we get sick of it
before then! I won't forgive you if we don't!

00:16:15.360 --> 00:16:16.680
We need to do it at least ten times!

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:18.630
Are you going to do it by yourself, Saki-chan?

00:16:18.630 --> 00:16:21.540
Are you out of your mind? You and I are going to...

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:27.240
I might as well go back to the office.

00:16:27.240 --> 00:16:31.520
K-Kucchii has classes to attend or something like that.

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:35.810
I shouldn't be wasting time.

00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:40.860
See you later.

00:16:46.430 --> 00:16:48.650
Ogiue-san, you should work on the plot.

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:50.100
Yeah, you're right.

00:17:02.190 --> 00:17:03.300
Excuse me.

00:17:05.730 --> 00:17:07.170
Have a seat.

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:07.750
Yes, sir.

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:12.360
Tell us your name, the university you're
attending, and the school you're enrolled in.

00:17:12.980 --> 00:17:17.180
Sasahara Kanji, Shiiou University,
School of Literature,
Department of Historical Geography.

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:20.890
Please tell us a little about yourself in the next three minutes.

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:21.480
Okay.

00:17:22.400 --> 00:17:25.130
When I first enrolled in the university, I was a lethargic student.

00:17:25.590 --> 00:17:28.360
I didn't have any hobbies or skills.

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:31.090
I thought that I'd end up as a student with vague aspirations,

00:17:31.090 --> 00:17:38.500
one who nonchalantly took classes for four years and
found himself working in a company he didn't care for.

00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:39.580
Okay, thank you.

00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:41.810
Um... Okay.

00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:44.350
Sasahara-kun, which section do you want to work in?

00:17:44.800 --> 00:17:46.580
Manga editing.

00:17:46.930 --> 00:17:48.180
Wow, that's my section.

00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:53.490
That's unusual.
Most people want to go into current affairs or literature.

00:17:53.930 --> 00:17:54.630
Magazine?

00:17:55.030 --> 00:17:56.950
No, Beforenoon.

00:17:57.860 --> 00:17:58.350
Why?

00:17:59.000 --> 00:18:04.600
There's a diverse mix of genres and writers, which gives me the impression that you're open to all kinds of ideas.

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:05.500
Can you provide an example?

00:18:06.180 --> 00:18:11.810
You serialize titles like Subaru Kaidou,
which is a serious and hard-boiled piece of classical literature,

00:18:11.810 --> 00:18:14.280
while also handling moe titles like Easy Trouble.

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:18.040
This potpourri, which may not be the best choice of words,

00:18:18.040 --> 00:18:22.700
comes off as an aggressive attitude that isn't present in
other magazines. It exemplifies your will to nurture artists.

00:18:23.300 --> 00:18:27.380
It's not like Magazine and Yoshiyoshi don't develop artists, too.

00:18:27.380 --> 00:18:28.770
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:34.170
What I meant to say was that Beforenoon
seems to assert that attitude more than the others.

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:36.590
Have you ever written a manga?

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:43.350
Yes. Well, I've never drawn one,
but I helped create one from a producer's standpoint.

00:18:43.800 --> 00:18:44.640
What was the topic?

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:48.080
Kuroki Yuu-sensei's Kujibiki Unbalance.

00:18:49.330 --> 00:18:50.790
A parody? R-18?

00:18:51.280 --> 00:18:52.540
B-Both.

00:18:54.070 --> 00:18:59.090
After the doujinshi was made,
I gained an even greater appreciation for the original manga.

00:19:01.290 --> 00:19:04.100
Sasahara-kun, what do you think about copyrights?

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:06.260
The other day,

00:19:06.260 --> 00:19:10.050
a person who wrote the final episode of Nekozaemon without permission had charges pressed against him.

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:12.400
What do you think about that?

00:19:13.060 --> 00:19:13.860
Well...

00:19:15.140 --> 00:19:18.670
It's common belief that doujinshis and
publishing companies are in a mutual relationship.

00:19:19.370 --> 00:19:23.220
There are several artists who ask
readers to write and submit doujinshis.

00:19:23.610 --> 00:19:28.370
However, by joining our company,
you'll be responsible for restricting that kind of activity.

00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:31.890
Do you have any thoughts about that?

00:19:33.610 --> 00:19:36.140
I'm sorry. I'm afraid I don't understand the question.

00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:40.160
Kujiun certainly is an interesting title.

00:19:40.160 --> 00:19:42.990
I've read all of Kuroki-sensei's works.

00:19:43.470 --> 00:19:49.960
However, I have a hard time believing that
it's an appropriate title to base a doujinshi on.

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:56.550
Sasahara-kun, you're seeking a position in editing,
but it doesn't sound like you have a clear stance on doujinshis.

00:19:57.230 --> 00:19:59.930
We would have liked to hear your position regarding that topic.

00:20:00.440 --> 00:20:02.760
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to.

00:20:03.880 --> 00:20:06.930
Sasahara-kun, I get the impression that you're a nice guy,

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:09.020
serious and a little naïve.

00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:11.350
I can tell just by looking at you.

00:20:12.410 --> 00:20:17.210
If I had the opportunity to know you better,
Sasahara-kun, I'd be able to see your virtues.

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:22.490
Having said that,
I'm not interviewing people for a position as a friend.

00:20:23.230 --> 00:20:26.330
I'm conducting these interviews in
order to look for partners to work with.

00:20:27.490 --> 00:20:29.640
When I asked you to describe yourself,

00:20:30.260 --> 00:20:36.220
did you really think I'd want to work with
someone who describes himself as an underachiever?

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:40.990
Thank you very much.

00:20:59.990 --> 00:21:04.020
<i>You're really useless!
Why did you have to give up?</i>

00:21:04.440 --> 00:21:06.010
<i>Take this! Take this!</i>

00:21:06.010 --> 00:21:08.840
<i>It hurts! It hurts! It hurts, Menma-chan!</i>

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:19.500
<i>I'm only helping him because he's
stupid and pathetic... It feels so good!</i>

00:21:20.600 --> 00:21:25.220
<i>I was thinking about something else... I'm coming! I'm coming! I'm coming!</i>

00:23:11.200 --> 00:23:14.560
Check! Check! Check it in your hearts!
Check it on your VCR!

00:23:14.560 --> 00:23:15.830
It sounds like you're having fun.

00:23:15.830 --> 00:23:18.750
It's because the next episode is by the original author!

00:23:18.750 --> 00:23:20.700
That's a common trend these days,

00:23:20.700 --> 00:23:21.950
not that I care about it.

00:23:21.950 --> 00:23:24.330
What do you say?
What's the meaning of this?

00:23:24.330 --> 00:23:25.920
Isn't that a great thing?

00:23:25.920 --> 00:23:27.670
If the quality is great, shower it with praise.

00:23:27.670 --> 00:23:29.980
If it isn't, let your imagination run wild.

00:23:29.980 --> 00:23:33.550
Think about the kind of procedures, negotiations, retakes, reservations, betrayals,

00:23:33.550 --> 00:23:36.560
and tirades that might have taken place!

00:23:36.560 --> 00:23:38.830
I already know you're looking forward to it.
